course: dictionary
lesson: 5573
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one to use. Read the clues before you choose. «With new glasses the letters are sharp again» means the signs on the board, because glasses help you see shapes clearly, not messages.
explain: Now look at «Paul wrote letters to churches». Here a letter is a written message sent to people, not a sign of the alphabet. Ask yourself: what would fit in this spot? A message fits, so that is the meaning to use.
explain: In maths, a letter can stand for a number we do not know yet. In x + 3 = 7, the x is a letter that hides the number 4. «To the letter» means exactly as you were told, so doing a task to the letter means doing it exactly right.
fact: A letter is one of the signs we use to write words, such as A, b or Z.
fact: A letter is also a written message you send to someone, usually in an envelope by post.
fact: In maths, a letter such as x or n can stand for an unknown number.
fact: «To the letter» means exactly as you were told.
fact: Capital letters and small letters are different signs for the same letter, so «A» and «a» are both the letter A.
exercise: «The letters on the board were sharp again after Sam got new glasses.» What are the letters here? | An unknown number | *Signs we use to write words, like A or b | A message sent in an envelope | A kind of paper
exercise: «Paul wrote letters to churches.» What does letter mean here? | Exactly as told | *A written message sent to people | A sign like A or b | An unknown number
exercise: In x + 3 = 7, what is x? | A written message | *A letter standing for an unknown number | A word spelled backwards | A capital letter in a name
test: «He did the task to the letter, exactly as his teacher had told him.» What does to the letter mean? | Quickly and loudly | *Exactly as told | Only half finished | Very carefully written with a pen
test: Vikings wrote with runes, which were letters of straight lines cut into wood and stone. What were runes mostly used for? | Magic spells | *Writing | Counting sheep | Painting pictures
exam: In «Many list words are common in letters and formal writing», what does letters mean? | Unknown numbers | Signs we use to write words | *Written messages sent to people | Exactly as told
